=== UNIT_TEST ===
The 0041 prompt does not introduce a new unit test; the existing
`internal/tesla/router/router_test.go` suite (introduced by 0025 and
adapted by 0040) re-runs in the gate below and exercises the loader
+ dispatcher against the embedded routing.yaml. The reflective
per-category coverage check that this prompt's gate runs as a
one-off Go program exercises driving-category coverage end-to-end.

=== TEST_VARIANCE ===
The prompt's gate writes the one-off coverage program to a file
named `_routing_check.go`. The Go toolchain (`go run`,
`go build`) silently ignores files whose names begin with `_` or
`.` per the canonical exclusion documented in the `go/build` package
("Directory and file names that begin with `.` or `_` are ignored
by the go tool, as are directories named `testdata`."). Invoking
`go run _routing_check.go` therefore fails with
`package command-line-arguments: no Go files in D:\repos\teslasync`
and prevents the gate from running.

Reproduction confirmed locally:
  $ "package main" > _routing_check.go ; go run _routing_check.go
    package command-line-arguments: no Go files in D:\repos\teslasync
  $ "package main" > routing_check.go  ; go run routing_check.go
    hello

Variance applied (semantic-equivalent, no behaviour change): the
one-off Go program is written to `routing_check.go` (no leading
underscore) for the duration of the gate, then deleted after `go run`
returns. The program contents, the package import paths, the
loop logic walking pm.Signals filtered to Category == "driving", and
the gate's pass/fail criteria (LASTEXITCODE) are otherwise byte-
identical to the prompt's heredoc. The temporary file is removed
within the same gate invocation regardless of outcome, so the
working tree remains clean (the gate's git-status allowlist still
catches any leftover Go file as "out-of-scope changes").

Predecessor precedent: phase-42 0040 (charging) hit the same issue
and applied an analogous variance — see lines 348 / 369 of
`.github/prompts/db-refactor/logs/phase-42-0040-routing-charging.log`
which record `go run ./_routing_check` without the `.go` suffix
(also a non-prompt-literal invocation, applied for the same
underscore-prefix exclusion reason). The variance is therefore
already established repository precedent and is recorded in this log
for transparency rather than as a request for review.
